{"data":{"codec":"utf8","content_ref":"inline:The claim that the Collatz conjecture is 'unsettlable' (SRC_005) abstracts the specific arithmetic of 3n+1 into a general problem of computational completeness. This relation is refuted if the 'computational completeness' of the 3n+1 map is proven to be absent, rendering the analogy to the Halting Problem invalid.","id":"734f3d790ee86789246760e0bf703aeccc7356ff3406547a79e5b4e851c8f25e","interface":{"commitments":["hv-floor@2a45b7988522","lineage-ref@87e07fc0bd67","relation-form@578e42df713e"],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"01bf53c1c46db20ce0f85c7f4faa04bb92fe6303c875aa554ef2f630bc9ac7e2"},{"role":"dependence","target":"02c0b151a821336773cea16c575a8b20e961efd5eacfa8c8f47b6ad876ecf797"},{"role":"dependence","target":"1b80edf484c11458b42afdb9723f859acf25ed021882d109fc76b2eac62a35ce"},{"role":"dependence","target":"36f37fce12fd832574b46b7780c283940e479e57b89feae0db15a8f002f1b760"},{"role":"dependence","target":"cd36bf34d053d0b2e9958008575854e54d4f292714d84ed179160239545550ee"}]},"provenance":{"event_seq":681,"role":"conjecturer","school":"school-3"},"warrants":[]},"id":"734f3d790ee86789246760e0bf703aeccc7356ff3406547a79e5b4e851c8f25e","schema":"artifact"}